    "instanceId": "EX-CORE-U4-36-P01-speak",
    "revision": 1,
    "title": "Speaking and interaction practice",
    "subtitle": "Choosing between close alternatives · 1 · preparation 1",
    "context": "Use this subset of the qualities vocabulary and constructions in a short self-contained situation, preparing for U4-36. Use the selected vocabulary and constructions to compare qualities and justify a selection with concrete evidence.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U4-36-P01-speak-produce",
        "kind": "check",
        "title": "Explain the situation",
        "questions": [
          {
            "id": "EX-CORE-U4-36-P01-speak-draft",
            "kind": "production",
            "response": "spoken",
            "prompt": "Choosing between close alternatives · 1 · preparation 1: Explain the situation to someone who heard only the initial account. Clarify what changed, give a supported reason, and distinguish the participants’ stated intentions from assumptions.",
            "promptLanguage": "en",
            "context": "星期六，班里约好一起去图书馆。哥哥看见手机上的消息写着九点，就告诉朋友不用太早出门。朋友却说，老师刚刚说的是八点半。\n\n哥哥觉得朋友记错了，所以把手机上的消息拿给他看。朋友认真看了日期，才发现那是上个月不同的一次活动的消息，并不是这次的安排。\n\n哥哥有点儿不好意思，说自己没有认真看。他重新找到这次的通知，问清楚是八点半在学校门口见面，再一起坐车去图书馆。\n\n他马上把正确时间告诉已经听过旧消息的同学，没有只在心里记住错误。大家都及时改了安排，没有人因此晚到。\n\n活动结束后，哥哥把旧通知放到别的地方，提醒自己以后先看清楚日期。这次虽然看错了，他却没有因此觉得自己以后什么都做不好。\n\n朋友说，愿意说出自己的错误，再把对的告诉别人，比一直说自己记得准有用。哥哥点头，下一次告诉别人消息之前，他会先把时间和地点都看清楚。",
            "contextLanguage": "zh",
            "label": "Take your speaking turn",
            "resultDomain": "Self-reviewed speaking practice",
            "rubric": [
              {
                "id": "r1",
                "text": "I retained the change or contrast that matters to the outcome."
              },
              {
                "id": "r2",
                "text": "I kept stated intentions separate from my assumptions."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "sequential": true
      }
